<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via $1.0 billion customer RP's.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via $1.0 billion customer RP's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of New York added reserves to the banking system via $1.0 billion customer repurchase agreements, a Fed spokesman said.</p>
<p>The move was a little bit of a surprise since most analysts were expecting the Fed to refrain from market operations on Friday. They said, however, the move has no monetary policy implications.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the time when the Fed usually intervenes in the market, fed funds were trading at 5-1/4 percent, in line with the Fed's target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1676</p>
